    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed"><strong>Status.</strong> This paper states a thesis, fifteen hypotheses (H1 to H15), six falsifiers and a programme of work, accompanied by interactive instruments at <a href="/living/rce-jepa/">/living/rce-jepa/</a>. Its measured results now cover the Phase 0 deterministic floors (the Form corpus and H1, the adversarial fuzzed arm of H7, the six-target determinism streams of H8, and the deterministic repair ladder of H14), the local Apple M5 Max checker-versus-model <code>reported_j</code> ratio <strong>H2</strong> (<code>C_check / E_model = 0.000582 &lt;= 0.05</code>, <code>1,718</code> times cheaper), single-shot and bounded checker-feedback <strong>H15</strong> across the <strong>40 open residual tasks</strong> (<code>17/40</code> to <code>34/40</code> single-shot; <strong><code>40/40</code> (<code>100.0%</code>)</strong> under bounded <code>&lt;= 5</code>-turn checker feedback plus public standard-library signature headers in <code>H15-Iterative</code> on <code>Claude Opus 5.5</code> and <code>Claude Sonnet 5.5</code> with <code>0</code> contradictions, <code>39/40</code> on <code>xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning</code>, and <strong><code>40/40</code> zero-call replay</strong> at <code>0.325 µs</code> / <code>1.77 µJ</code> from memory-mapped Gear-0), the purpose-trained latent Form JEPA repair proposer <strong><code>FormJEPA-v1</code></strong> (<code>8.42M</code> trainable parameters over disjoint Form S-expressions, admitting <code>177/200</code> held-out synthetic defects and <code>27/40</code> residual tasks at <code>k = 16</code>, cutting recurring <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> Gear-2 episodes from <code>200</code> to <code>12</code>, <code>16.67×</code>, with <code>200/200</code> stream admissions when paired with <code>H15-Iterative</code>), the contrastive multi-step margin energy-based model (EBM) scorer <strong><code>FormEBM-v2</code></strong> (<code>5.85M</code> trainable parameters on the identical strictly disjoint <code>1,387</code>-Form split, lifting unseen-shape <strong>H5</strong> area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) from <code>0.618</code> to <strong><code>0.8922 &gt;= 0.85</code></strong> with <code>84.05%</code> solvable top-1 accuracy and <code>2.39×</code> fewer checker calls, and lifting unseen-chain <strong>H11</strong> strict 5-step edit monotonicity from <code>36.0%</code> to <strong><code>93.0% &gt;= 80%</code></strong> at Spearman <code>0.9931</code> and <code>47.09 mJ</code>/candidate core <code>reported_j</code>), the span-normalized two-head decomposed scorer <strong><code>FormEBM-v3</code></strong> (<code>6.05M</code> trainable parameters on the identical split, raising unseen-shape <strong>H5</strong> AUROC to <strong><code>0.9437 &gt;= 0.85</code></strong> with <code>83.44%</code> defect-head and <code>80.98%</code> composite solvable top-1 accuracy, raising unseen-chain <strong>H11</strong> strict 5-step monotonicity to <strong><code>94.0%</code></strong> on <code>E_depth</code> at Spearman <code>0.9966</code> and <strong><code>92.0%</code></strong> on <code>E_total</code> at Spearman <code>0.9846</code>, and eliminating Wave-4 cross-task edit-span inversion on zero-shot out-of-distribution (OOD) <strong>H15</strong> by lifting multi-proposer pooled AUROC from <code>0.2585</code> to <strong><code>0.5278</code></strong> and large-span valid versus short invalid AUROC to <strong><code>0.6018</code></strong> at <code>232.45 mJ</code>/candidate core <code>reported_j</code>), and the pre-registered 151-task <strong><code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code></strong> promotion audit (<code>3/119 = 2.5% &gt; 2.0%</code> stochastic share, <code>3/3</code> passing <code>W-MUT-1</code>, <code>0</code> contradictions, confirming rung <code>f</code> remains in <code>observe</code> mode). Honest disclosure: full intent-to-Form synthesis (H3), end-to-end joule parity (H4), cross-module signature-and-trace OOD energy calibration beyond <code>0.5278</code> across multi-module git-history rewrites, reference-app encoding (H6), cost-table prediction (H9), quotient data-saving (H10), decision-head calibration (H12), discrete-versus-continuous long-horizon planning (H13), diffusion/evolutionary H15 arms, and external wall-meter <code>measured_j</code> remain open. JEPA is the premise: predict a summary of meaning, not the surface text. The subject is World Coding, any learned proposer over Forms, with the Laws of Coding as the acceptance rule. The deciding half (commit gate, exact replay, projection, and integer cost units) is described in <a href="/papers/rce/">the RCE paper</a>; this paper is about the proposer: a learned model that steers search over Forms while the engine renders every target. Any model in the loop, hosted or local, only proposes, and security never depends on it.</p>

