    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">In plain words</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>The subject is World Coding. A World of Code is the space of program Forms, plus exact rules for the next state and for what is accepted (the Laws of Coding). JEPA is the premise, not the whole method: predict a summary of meaning instead of the next word of code. AI (artificial intelligence) here means any learned proposer, not one architecture.</li>
        <li>The model proposes and the checker decides. Trace-trained decoders, diffusion, reinforcement learning inside a proof checker, evolutionary search, library learning and constrained decoding can all sit in that slot. The gate does not change when the proposer does. Safety does not depend on the proposer being right.</li>
        <li>Measured floors and residual benchmarks stay strictly labeled. Over 185 hand-written programs the median description-length ratio is 9.34 (H1); on Apple M5 Max at commit <code>1762fb4b</code>, checking a Form costs <code>49.04 mJ</code> against <code>84.25 J</code> per local 35B candidate generation (<code>1,718×</code> cheaper, supporting H2); fuzzed checks found 0 broken invariants in 1,275 accepted mutants (H7); replay matched on 10,500 streams across six targets (H8); and the deterministic ladder closed 111 of 151 tasks (73.5%) with zero model calls, leaving 40 real-history tasks (H14). Across those 40 residual tasks (H15), single-shot proposers admit <code>17/40</code> to <code>34/40</code>, bounded checker feedback with public standard-library headers (<code>H15-Iterative</code>, zero access to the original Form) closes <strong><code>40/40</code> (<code>100.0%</code>)</strong> on <code>Claude Opus 5.5</code> and <code>Claude Sonnet 5.5</code> with <code>0</code> contradictions (<code>39/40</code> on <code>xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning</code>) and crystallizes <strong><code>40/40</code> into Gear 0 (<code>DNULLMM1</code>)</strong> for zero-call replay, purpose-trained <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> (<code>8.42M</code> parameters) admits <code>27/40</code> at <code>k = 16</code> while contrastive <code>FormEBM-v2</code> (<code>5.85M</code> parameters: AUROC <code>0.8922</code>, <code>93.0%</code> monotonicity) and span-normalized <code>FormEBM-v3</code> (<code>6.05M</code> parameters: unseen-shape AUROC <code>0.9437</code> on H5, <code>94.0%</code> <code>E_depth</code> / <code>92.0%</code> <code>E_total</code> monotonicity on H11, and zero-shot H15 pooled AUROC lifted from <code>0.2585</code> to <code>0.5278</code>) rank Form candidates without invoking the checker, and the <strong>3-Gear Cascade</strong> admits <code>200/200</code> recurring <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> arrivals with <code>16.67×</code> fewer frontier episodes (<code>12</code> vs <code>200</code>). <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> stays in <code>observe</code> mode (<code>3/119 = 2.5% &gt; 2.0%</code>, <code>0</code> contradictions), and no external wall-meter reading (<code>measured_j</code>) is claimed.</li>
      </ol>
