    <p><strong>Lane reading.</strong> The training reports above move toward semantics: execution traces, environment dynamics, and rewards a checker can see. The test suite is still the oracle, and PatchDiff is evidence that a test suite is incomplete. SWE-Bench Pro's board is higher than its launch text and still grades patches by tests. That is the opening the Laws of Coding name. An exact checker replaces "tests passed" with an accepted Form. Acceptance is part of the world, not a score fitted afterward.</p>

    <h3 id="lane-hybrids">3.2 Creative hybrids</h3>
    <p>This lane pairs a learned proposer with a gate that already exists: an evaluator, a proof kernel, a type system, or a set of examples.</p>
