    <p id="h14-result"><strong>H14, measured.</strong> The ladder is <code>rce repair</code> of openIE-dev/rce, with the rungs of the proposer section above and an enumeration bound of 2000 candidates. It has three runs, each registered before it ran, and together they are the current result. Run 1 [B30] closed 118 of 120 tasks with zero model calls, but 119 of its 120 tasks were operator and integer-literal mutations, which bounded enumeration inverts by construction, and 9 of the 118 closures pass the examples and checks without being the original program. Run 2 [B31] has no operator or literal mutation: 41 changes from the git history of openIE-dev/rce, 27 guard negations and 83 renames, 151 tasks in all. It closed 31 of them (20.5%) with zero model calls: 1 of the 41 history tasks; all 27 guard negations, every one by the enumeration edit that removes a <code>not</code>, which inverts that mutation by construction; and 3 of the 83 renames, none of them restored to the original. Of the 41 history tasks, 39 are programs updated because the language changed, not defects; only 2 are defects of a program, and the ladder closed one of them. Without the guard negations, 4 of 124 tasks close (3.2%). Run 2's prediction P3, that 10% to 40% of the renames close, failed, and its falsifier F1 was met: the closure rate of run 1 does not carry over to changes from real history. Run 3 [B32] ran run 2's 151 tasks unchanged, at openIE-dev/rce <code>8a5d90ea</code>, with rung 5, renames, after rung 4; its registration records that renames are the class rung 5 was built for after run 2. Its plain arm, the ladder given only the task, closed 111 of 151 (73.5%) with zero model calls, 103 of them restored to the original: all 83 renames (80 at rung 5, 3 at rung 4), 77 of them restored; all 27 guard negations, each with its outcome in run 2; and 1 of the 41 history tasks, the same one as in run 2. Without the guard negations, 84 of 124 tasks close (67.7%). Its known-good arm gave the ladder each task's original program as well: it closed 116 of 151, 114 restored, including all 83 renames restored and 6 of the 41 history tasks. Run 3's prediction P6, that in the known-good arm every guard and history task keeps its plain-arm outcome, failed: 5 more history tasks close, and the one closed in the plain arm closes at rung 5 instead of rung 3. None of run 3's six falsifiers was met, and the ladder reported zero model calls in both arms. H14's registered rule is support at 10% or more of the registered tasks, and falsification below 10%, for the share the public deterministic ladder closes with zero model calls, every closure admitted by the checker, at a frozen ladder commit. The plain arm meets those conditions. By the rule, H14 is supported: the plain arm of run 3 closes 111 of 151 (73.5%), leaving 40 open residual tasks from git history.</p>

    <p id="h15-result"><strong>H2, single-shot H15, and Shape D (<code>DNULLMM1</code>) Gear-0 on the 40 open residual tasks, measured [B33].</strong> Registered prior to execution (<code>rce-jepa-h15-and-shape-d-gear0-2026-11-22</code>, <code>sha256: b64c4c671ae85755...</code>) against <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (<code>2026-11-20</code>, binary <code>sha256: 1d3b0d07ff5b2e8f...</code>), the 40 residual tasks (<code>sha256: 3ca3a32769145e9b...</code>; <code>25</code> <code>W-SYN-1</code>, <code>5</code> <code>W-LEN-1</code>, <code>4</code> <code>W-NAME-1,W-TY-1</code>, <code>3</code> <code>W-NAME-1</code>, <code>1</code> <code>W-WORLD-1</code>, <code>1</code> <code>W-CAP-3,W-WORLD-1</code>, <code>1</code> <code>W-INT-1</code>) were evaluated under strict gate predicate <code>C(z) = 1</code>: (1) <code>rce check candidate.rce</code> exits <code>0</code> (enforcing <code>W-UI-1</code> and <code>W-MUT-1</code> non-vacuity), (2) <code>no_spec_deletion</code> preserves all declared <code>state</code>, <code>event</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>struct</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>fn</code>, <code>extern</code>, and <code>step</code> headers plus every <code>example</code> left-hand-side trace and <code>check</code> count of the mutant, and (3) secondary equivalence audit via <code>rce hash</code> (<code>restored</code>), <code>rce equiv fuel 2000</code> (<code>behaviour-equal</code>), and <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> <code>observe</code> mode.</p>

