    <p id="form-jepa-and-rung-f-result"><strong><code>FormJEPA-v1</code> latent Form repair proposer, 3-Gear Cascade, and 151-task <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> promotion audit, measured [B34].</strong> Pre-registered before dataset generation, weight initialization, and rung-<code>f</code> execution (<code>rce-jepa-form-jepa-v1-2026-11-22</code>, <code>sha256: 22682e6e936ec120...</code>; <code>rce-repair-rung-f-wave3-eval-2026-11-22</code>, <code>sha256: 04aff4b2b44cdbea...</code>) against <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (Linux x86_64 binary <code>sha256: 5ef9931ff23a310f...</code>), <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> (<code>8,424,073</code> trainable parameters, <code>13,917,577</code> with EMA target buffers; checkpoint <code>sha256: cbfbf2274175c737...</code>) was trained from random initialization (<code>seed = 20261122</code>) on <code>6,329</code> checker-verified defect pairs across <code>1,106</code> disjoint valid Form shapes (extracted from <code>1,387</code> unique Form shapes after four-layer path, slug, declaration-name, and <code>458</code>-digest <code>rce fmt nameless</code> exclusion with <code>0</code> overlap against the 151 ladder or 40 residual tasks). It pairs a 6-layer Pre-LN Transformer context encoder (<code>d = 256</code>) over quotient-normalized Form AST S-expression tokens with an EMA target encoder (<code>τ = 0.996</code>), a 3-layer residual MLP latent predictor trained under Smooth-L<sub>1</sub> plus VICReg variance-covariance anti-collapse regularization (raising context effective rank from <code>32.90</code> at epoch 0 to <strong><code>85.24</code></strong> post-training, coordinate standard deviation <code>0.1038</code> to <code>0.3830</code>, and positive-pair latent L<sub>2</sub> energy from <code>149.25</code> to <code>10.57</code> versus <code>13.02</code> random-pair), and a 2-layer latent-conditioned typed edit decoder reranked by <code>||z_hat_y - E_ema(y_cand)||_2^2</code>.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Disjoint synthetic, 151-ladder, and 40-residual accuracy versus model scale:</strong> On <code>200</code> held-out disjoint synthetic Form defects (unseen <code>shape_hash</code>es), <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> admits <strong><code>156/200</code> (<code>78.0%</code>)</strong> at <code>k = 1</code> and <strong><code>177/200</code> (<code>88.5%</code>)</strong> at <code>k = 16</code>. On the 151-task ladder (plain arm), standalone <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> admits <code>27/151</code> (<code>k = 1</code>) and <code>57/151</code> (<code>k = 16</code>), lifting the combined deterministic ladder (<code>111/151</code>) plus <code>FormJEPA-v1 (k = 16)</code> to <strong><code>138/151</code> (<code>91.4%</code>)</strong> with zero frontier calls. On the 40 open residual tasks (H15), <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> admits <strong><code>22/40</code> (<code>55.0%</code>)</strong> at <code>k = 1</code> and <strong><code>27/40</code> (<code>67.5%</code>)</strong> at <code>k = 16</code> (<code>25</code> restored + <code>2</code> behaviour-equal = <code>27/27</code> behaves-the-same, <code>5.33</code> mean <code>rce check</code> calls/task), matching local <code>Qwen 3.6 35B-A3B</code> (<code>27/40</code>) on structured grammar, length-method, and capability repairs (<code>24/25</code> <code>W-SYN-1</code>, <code>2/5</code> <code>W-LEN-1</code>, <code>1/1</code> <code>W-WORLD-1</code>), while closing <code>0/9</code> multi-module cryptographic stdlib migrations (<code>W-NAME-1</code> / <code>W-TY-1</code> across <code>hpke</code>, <code>mls</code>, <code>pq</code>, <code>pqxdh</code>, <code>energy</code>), compound <code>W-CAP-3,W-WORLD-1</code>, and vacuous-example synthesis tasks where Gear-2 frontier proposers remain required.</li>
      <li><strong>Inference <code>reported_j</code>, 3-Gear Cascade, and honest H5/H11 diagnostics:</strong> On AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 Linux <code>powercap</code> RAPL counters (<code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>, <code>derived_marginal_pkg_reported_j = None</code> under Falsifier 6 at <code>33.38%</code> co-tenant package drift), per-proposal CPU inference costs <strong><code>58.65 mJ</code></strong> RAPL core (<code>1.194 J</code> gross package, <code>10.15 ms</code>) at <code>k = 1</code> and <strong><code>474.76 mJ</code></strong> RAPL core (<code>6.736 J</code> gross package, <code>67.51 ms</code>) at <code>k = 16</code> — <code>70.6×</code> to <code>1,436×</code> lower at <code>k = 1</code> (<code>12.5×</code> to <code>177.5×</code> at <code>k = 16</code>) than one local 35B candidate (<code>84.25 J</code>). Inserting <code>FormJEPA-v1 (k = 16)</code> as Gear 1 between <code>DNULLMM1</code> Gear 0 and <code>Claude Opus 5.5</code> Gear 2 preserves <code>34/40</code> single-pass closure while cutting <code>Opus 5.5</code> calls from <code>40</code> to <code>13</code> (<code>$1.38</code> to <code>$0.81</code>), and on the 200-arrival <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> stream cuts Gear-2 frontier calls from <code>200</code> (stateless) and <code>48</code> (2-Gear) to <strong><code>23</code> calls (<code>8.70×</code> reduction; <code>152</code> Gear-0 hits, <code>25</code> Gear-1 admissions, <code>7</code> Gear-2 admissions)</strong>; with local <code>Qwen 3.6</code> as Gear 2, <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> 35B calls drop to <code>49</code> (<code>4.08×</code> reduction) and admitted arrivals rise from <code>141/200</code> to <code>154/200</code>. Uncalibrated negative latent L<sub>2</sub> distance alone achieves AUROC <strong><code>0.618</code></strong> across <code>925</code> beam candidates (H5 inconclusive: above <code>0.60</code> disproof floor, below <code>0.85</code> support threshold) and rises across cumulative edit distances <code>0..4</code> (<code>0.00, 0.99, 2.26, 3.27, 3.89</code>, then <code>3.72</code> at <code>d = 5</code>; <code>18/50 = 36.0% &lt; 80%</code> strict 5-step monotonicity on H11), showing that repair accuracy here comes from conditioning the typed edit decoder on <code>(z_x, z_hat_y)</code> rather than smooth uncalibrated latent energy alone.</li>
