    <p id="form-ebm-and-h15-iterative-result"><strong>Contrastive multi-step margin energy scorer (<code>FormEBM-v2</code>, H5 &amp; H11) and <code>40/40</code> bounded checker-feedback residual closure (<code>H15-Iterative</code> + Gear-0 v2), measured [B35].</strong> Pre-registered before corpus generation, weight initialization, and API execution (<code>rce-jepa-form-ebm-v2-2026-11-23</code>, <code>sha256: 128f17e69361ea89...</code>; <code>rce-jepa-h15-iterative-2026-11-23</code>, <code>sha256: a7774d3bd03ae450...</code>) against <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (Linux x86_64 binary <code>sha256: 331464496009d98a...</code>), two targeted evaluations tested whether (A) replacing uncalibrated coordinate distance with a contrastive + pairwise edit-depth margin energy head on the identical strictly disjoint <code>1,387</code>-Form split closes H5 and H11, and (B) supplying public <code>stdlib/lib</code> module headers plus bounded deterministic checker diagnostics (<code>max_turns = 5</code>, zero access to <code>original</code>) closes the six remaining residual tasks from single-shot H15.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong><code>FormEBM-v2</code> architecture, tokenizer fix, and unseen-shape H5 / H11 results (<code>137</code> unseen test Form shapes, <code>0</code> overlap):</strong> Two structural causes explained why <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> reached only <code>0.618</code> AUROC on H5 and <code>36.0%</code> strict 5-step monotonicity on H11: its single-file S-expression tokenizer mapped both live unused bindings (<code>let x</code>, refused by <code>W-UNUSED-1</code>) and underscore-prefixed bindings (<code>let _x</code>, admitted) to the same <code>&lt;ID:k&gt;</code> slot while shifting subsequent <code>&lt;ID:j&gt;</code> indices whenever an unbound identifier appeared, and its coordinate Smooth-L<sub>1</sub> loss carried no contrastive validity or edit-depth margin. <code>FormEBM-v2</code> (<code>5,851,649</code> trainable parameters, checkpoint <code>sha256: 2204a0b9cbd0d96c...</code>; <code>857.2 s</code> training on AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 / Radeon 8060S APU at <code>5,375.0 J</code> core RAPL and <code>40,602.4 J</code> APU package RAPL) introduces reference-anchored <code>PairFormTokenizer</code> (<code>504</code> active tokens, distinguishing underscore-prefixed bindings, newly introduced identifier slots, and modulo-32 integer classes with purely syntactic diff tags and zero checker calls), a 5-layer shared Siamese Transformer, a 1-layer cross-attention RMS difference block, and a softplus energy head trained on <code>5,955</code> validity-margin triples (<code>m = 1.0</code>) and <code>600</code> 5-step cumulative corruption chains (<code>γ = 0.50(j − i)</code>) strictly over the <code>1,106</code> training Forms (VICReg effective rank expanding from <code>26.48</code> to <code>55.70</code> on <code>z_ref</code> and <code>46.44</code> to <code>74.72</code> on <code>z_cand</code>). On the <code>137</code> unseen held-out test Form shapes:
        <ul>
          <li><strong>H5 (<code>N = 200</code> unseen test beams, <code>3,064</code> candidates):</strong> Scalar energy reaches <strong>AUROC <code>0.8922 &gt;= 0.85</code></strong> (vs <code>0.6180</code> for <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> and <code>0.7208</code> for uncalibrated Siamese L<sub>2</sub>), lifting top-1 (<code>k = 1</code> without invoking <code>rce check</code> on beam items) valid selection from <code>22.5%</code> (<code>45/200</code> unreranked) and <code>25.0%</code> (<code>50/200</code> Siamese L<sub>2</sub>) to <strong><code>84.05%</code> on the <code>163</code> solvable beams (<code>137/163</code>; <code>68.50%</code> raw across all <code>200</code> beams)</strong> and cutting mean <code>rce check</code> invocations to first valid Form by <strong><code>2.39×</code></strong> (<code>3.577</code> to <code>1.497</code> checks/beam). Ten-thread CPU scoring costs <strong><code>47.09 mJ</code></strong> core RAPL per candidate (<code>6.30 ms</code>; <code>752.03 mJ</code> core and <code>11.88 J</code> gross package per 16-item beam, with <code>derived_marginal_pkg_reported_j = None</code> under Falsifier 6 at <code>13.7%</code> idle drift).</li>
          <li><strong>H11 (<code>N = 100</code> unseen 5-step cumulative defect chains):</strong> Strict 5-step monotonicity (<code>E_0 &lt; E_1 &lt; E_2 &lt; E_3 &lt; E_4 &lt; E_5</code>) rises from <code>36.0%</code> (<code>FormJEPA-v1</code>) and <code>18.0%</code> (Siamese L<sub>2</sub>) to <strong><code>93.0%</code> (<code>93/100 &gt;= 80%</code>)</strong>, with mean Spearman rank correlation <strong><code>ρ = 0.9931</code></strong> (median <code>1.0000</code>) and mean energy <code>[0.0007, 2.36, 5.16, 7.99, 12.21, 17.25]</code> across <code>d = 0..5</code> (zero <code>d = 5</code> rollover).</li>
          <li><strong>Candid domain boundaries:</strong> On unconstrained 5-step random walks (<code>N = 50</code>) that may overwrite an already-broken line twice without adding a new AST defect, mean energy still climbs <code>0.0007 → 7.07</code> (mean <code>ρ = 0.8513</code>, median <code>0.9429</code>), while strict step-by-step inequality is <code>38.0%</code> (<code>46.0%</code> non-decreasing). Zero-shot transfer to the OOD <code>40</code>-task git-history residual lifts within-task <code>k = 1</code> typed-edit admissions over <code>FormJEPA-v1</code> (<code>22/40 → 25/40</code>, beam capacity <code>30/40</code>), whereas pooled cross-task AUROC inverts to <code>0.2630</code> (<code>0.2585</code> across <code>332</code> multi-proposer candidates) because single-line edit-depth training assigns higher raw energy to large valid multi-line standard-library migrations than to 1-token syntax edits.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong><code>H15-Iterative</code> bounded checker feedback + public <code>stdlib/lib</code> headers (<code>40 / 40</code> closed, <code>0</code> contradictions, <code>40 / 40</code> Gear-0 replay):</strong> Supplying public declaration signatures (<code>pub const</code>, <code>pub struct</code>, <code>pub kind</code>, <code>pub fn</code> with bodies stripped, strictly excluding the task file itself) for imported <code>stdlib/lib</code> modules (<code>crypto.cat</code>, <code>crypto.unhex</code>, <code>crypto.tohex</code>, <code>core.bytes</code>, <code>pq</code>) plus verbatim deterministic <code>rce check</code> + <code>W-MUT-1</code> diagnostics up to <code>max_turns = 5</code> (with zero access to <code>original</code>) lifts admissions from <code>34/40</code> single-shot to <strong><code>40/40</code> (<code>100.0%</code>)</strong> on both <strong><code>Claude Opus 5.5</code></strong> (<code>38</code> at turn 1, <code>2</code> at turn 2; <code>42</code> calls, <code>$1.8104</code>, <code>34</code> restored + <code>5</code> behaviour-equal = <code>39</code> behaves-the-same, <strong><code>0</code> contradictions</strong>) and <strong><code>Claude Sonnet 5.5</code></strong> (<code>38</code> at turn 1, <code>1</code> at turn 2, <code>1</code> at turn 3; <code>43</code> calls, <strong><code>$1.1122</code></strong>, <code>35</code> restored + <code>4</code> behaviour-equal, <strong><code>0</code> contradictions</strong>), and to <strong><code>39/40</code> (<code>97.5%</code>)</strong> on <strong><code>xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning</code></strong> (<code>35</code> at turn 1, <code>2</code> at turn 2, <code>2</code> at turn 3; <code>50</code> calls, <code>$4.0555</code>, <strong><code>0</code> contradictions</strong>). All four previously unsolved cryptographic migrations (<code>stdlib/lib/hpke.rce</code>, <code>stdlib/lib/mls.rce</code>, <code>stdlib/lib/pq.rce</code>, <code>programs/ecosystem/pqxdh.rce</code>) were <strong>exact-hash <code>restored</code></strong> (at turn 1 on <code>Opus 5.5</code> and <code>Sonnet 5.5</code>; turns 1–3 on <code>Grok 4.20</code>), while both historical pre-<code>W-MUT-1</code> vacuous-example tasks (<code>57_float_vectors.rce</code>, <code>washer.rce</code>) closed with <strong><code>behaviour-equal</code></strong> under <code>rce equiv fuel 2000</code> (only <code>washer.rce</code> remained open on <code>Grok 4.20</code> after 5 turns). Crystallizing all 40 verified repairs into <code>DNULLMM1</code> Gear-0 v2 (<code>sha256: 80cf265038bcd5eb...</code>) replays <strong><code>40/40</code> (<code>100.0%</code>) at <code>0</code> model calls</strong>, and in the updated 3-Gear <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> stream (<code>M = 200</code> arrivals) admits <strong><code>200/200</code> (<code>100.0%</code>)</strong> of arrivals (<code>163</code> Gear-0 hits + <code>25</code> local Gear-1 admissions + <code>12</code> Gear-2 episodes / <code>14</code> API turns at <code>$0.9822</code>, a <strong><code>16.67×</code> episode reduction</strong> vs stateless <code>200</code> calls).</li>
