    <p id="form-ebm-v3-result"><strong>Span-normalized two-head decomposed scorer (<code>FormEBM-v3</code>, H5, H11, and zero-shot OOD H15 cross-span transfer), measured [B36].</strong> Pre-registered before synthetic multi-span pair generation, weight initialization, and evaluation (<code>rce-jepa-form-ebm-v3-2026-11-23</code>, <code>sha256: cb7ee1ac8dc5c594...</code>) against <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (Linux x86_64 binary <code>sha256: 386be0c26389550e...</code>), <code>FormEBM-v3</code> (<code>6,052,802</code> trainable parameters, pure-<code>float32</code> ROCm <code>Radeon 8060S</code> checkpoint <code>sha256: 71e642f1bb0b9c06...</code>; <code>2,528.3 s</code> training at <code>13,312.3 J</code> core RAPL and <code>48,422.2 J</code> APU package RAPL) tests whether decoupling defect validity from cumulative edit depth over the identical strictly disjoint <code>1,387</code>-Form split (<code>1,106</code> train, <code>144</code> validation, <code>137</code> unseen test shapes; <code>0</code> overlap with the 151 ladder or 40 H15 tasks, and <code>0</code> <code>rce check</code> calls during scoring) resolves <code>FormEBM-v2</code>'s cross-task OOD edit-size inversion (<code>0.2585</code>) without regressing H5 or H11:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Alignment-aware tokenization and two-head decomposition:</strong> <code>PairFormTokenizerv3</code> (<code>max_seq_len = 384</code>, <code>560</code> active tokens) replaces raw line-index comparison with line-shift-invariant sequence alignment, separates lexically bound/imported new identifiers (<code>&lt;BOUND_NEW_ID:0..31&gt;</code>) from unbound free symbols (<code>&lt;UNBOUND_NEW_ID:0..15&gt;</code>), and computes explicit normalized diff fraction <code>ρ_diff = Δ_tok / max(1, L_cand)</code>. Over the shared 5-layer Siamese encoder and cross-difference block, a span-invariant defect head <code>E_def(x, y, r) = softplus(g_def(feats_def))</code> (trained with within-beam plus all-pairs cross-task batch margin <code>m = 2.5</code> and L<sub>2</sub> positive anchor across <code>4,983</code> pairs including <code>219</code> <code>k = 2..10</code> multi-span valid rewrites strictly from <code>train_forms</code>) is separated from a cumulative corruption-depth head <code>E_depth(y_0, y_d) = softplus(g_depth(feats_depth))</code>, combined via <code>E_total = E_def + 0.15 · E_depth / log2(2 + Δ_tok)</code> (VICReg effective rank <code>42.79</code> on <code>z_ref</code> and <code>57.93</code> on <code>z_cand</code>, coordinate standard deviation <code>0.3332 / 0.3113 &gt;= 0.25</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Strengthened unseen-shape H5 (<code>0.9437</code>) and unseen-chain H11 (<code>94.0%</code> / <code>92.0%</code>):</strong> On the <code>200</code> unseen held-out test beams (<code>3,064</code> candidates), <code>FormEBM-v3</code> lifts <strong>H5 AUROC from <code>0.8922</code> (<code>FormEBM-v2</code>) to <code>0.9437 &gt;= 0.85</code></strong> (<code>0.9386</code> on <code>E_def</code> alone, reaching <code>TPR = 78.9%</code> at <code>FPR = 4.6%</code>), achieves <strong><code>83.44%</code> (<code>136/163</code>, <code>E_def</code>) and <code>80.98%</code> (<code>132/163</code>, <code>E_total</code>) solvable top-1 accuracy</strong> (both <code>&gt;= 80.0%</code>; <code>1.601</code> / <code>1.669</code> mean <code>rce check</code> calls vs <code>3.577</code> unreranked), and lifts <strong>H11 strict 5-step monotonicity on <code>100</code> unseen corruption chains to <code>94.0%</code> on <code>E_depth</code> (Spearman <code>ρ = 0.9966</code>, median <code>1.0000</code>) and <code>92.0%</code> on <code>E_total</code> (<code>ρ = 0.9846</code>, median <code>1.0000</code>)</strong>. Ten-thread CPU scoring at <code>max_seq_len = 384</code> costs <code>232.45 mJ</code> core RAPL per candidate (<code>32.55 ms</code>, <code>362×</code> lower than local 35B generation; <code>derived_marginal_pkg_reported_j = None</code> at <code>37.7%</code> co-tenant package drift).</li>
      <li><strong>Zero-shot OOD H15 inversion resolved (<code>0.2585 → 0.5278</code>), and candid cross-module boundary:</strong> Transferred zero-shot to the <code>40</code>-task git-history residual (<code>303</code> multi-proposer candidates including all <code>40/40</code> closed multi-hundred-line <code>hpke</code>, <code>mls</code>, <code>pq</code>, and <code>pqxdh</code> migrations), <code>FormEBM-v3</code> lifts pooled cross-task AUROC from <code>0.2585</code> (<code>FormEBM-v2</code>) to <strong><code>0.5278</code></strong> (<code>+0.2693</code>, clearing Falsifier F4 <code>&gt; 0.50</code>; <strong><code>0.6018</code></strong> on large-span valid rewrites with <code>Δ_tok &gt;= 10</code> vs short <code>0/1</code>-token invalid candidates, and <code>0.2630 → 0.4985</code> on the <code>286</code>-item typed-edit pool), while reaching <strong><code>27/40</code> multi-proposer and <code>24/40</code> typed-edit within-task <code>k = 1</code> admissions under <code>E_def</code></strong> (<code>25/40</code> and <code>22/40</code> under <code>E_total</code>, cutting mean typed-beam checks from <code>5.55</code> to <code>5.10</code>). On the 279-line <code>stdlib/lib/hpke.rce</code> migration (<code>Δ_tok = 146</code>), valid energy drops to <code>E_total = 0.9645</code> (<code>E_def = 0.8826</code>), yet across unseen multi-module cryptographic APIs (<code>mls.rce</code>, <code>pq.rce</code>, <code>pqxdh.rce</code>) and vacuous-example obligations (<code>washer.rce</code>), zero-shot pooled calibration plateaus near <code>0.53</code> because single-file syntax without imported <code>stdlib/lib</code> type signatures or exact <code>rce trace</code> rollouts cannot verify cross-module call contracts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="falsifiers">Falsifiers RJ-F1 to RJ-F6 for the premise itself</h3>
    <p>Each falsifier is an observation that would defeat part of the premise; several are stated in terms of the hypotheses above (RJ-F3 on H3, RJ-F4 on H11, RJ-F6 on H3 and H10).</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse [&_td]:border [&_th]:border [&_td]:border-brand-border [&_th]:border-brand-border [&_td]:p-2 [&_th]:p-2 [&_th]:text-left [&_th]:text-brand-white">
      <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Observation</th><th>What it defeats</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>RJ-F1</td><td>Lift coverage plateaus below 80% on any of the five target languages after the construct list is exhausted</td><td>The claim that all code can be emitted from RCE, and with it the scope of autonomous coding over Forms</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RJ-F2</td><td>Writing σ(I) for the 7 reference applications costs more person-hours than writing their Forms by hand</td><td>The claim that closure removes, rather than moves, the specification cost</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RJ-F3</td><td>H3 fails while the token arm passes at the same gate</td><td>Latent proposal over Form space; the gate still stands, the JEPA half does not</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RJ-F4</td><td>H11 fails and search does not reach accepted Forms within the beam budget</td><td>Energy-guided planning in Form space (not triggered on unseen cumulative 1..5-defect chains: <code>FormEBM-v2</code> reaches <code>93.0%</code> and <code>FormEBM-v3</code> reaches <code>94.0%</code> <code>E_depth</code> / <code>92.0%</code> <code>E_total</code> strict monotonicity with <code>0.9437</code> H5 AUROC; cross-module signature/trace OOD energy calibration beyond <code>0.5278</code> remains open)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RJ-F5</td><td>The decision head's calibration never beats a frequency table over shape hashes</td><td>The decision-model leg; it adds nothing over promoted-handler statistics</td></tr>
        <tr><td>RJ-F6</td><td>A token-space model trained with execution traces, of the CWM class, closes the residual of 40 tasks from the plain arm of H14 run 3, at equal energy and with the same gate as the acceptance rule</td><td>The claim that the Form quotient adds something for proposers during training/proposal (note: for Gear-0 reuse, <code>rce fmt nameless</code> already recovers <code>7/9</code> alpha-renamings at 0 calls; trained-proposer parity against H3/H10 awaits a trained JEPA arm)</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>

    <p>The thesis is disproved overall if H4 fails (no joule advantage per accepted program) or H6 fails (the Form cannot express the reference apps). Either alone is sufficient.</p>

    <h3>What will be delivered</h3>
    <p>Scope, organised as parallel workstreams that meet at the evaluation harness. Every deliverable either produces Forms, produces models that propose Forms, or measures the result.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>W1. Form corpus and dataset card.</strong> Forms paired with intent statements and checker verdicts, from hand-written Forms, reference-app Forms and checker-verified mutations; the card covers provenance, licence, size distribution, negative generation, known gaps and contamination controls; canonical serialization for H1.</li>
      <li><strong>W2. Encoder and predictor.</strong> Intent encoder, EMA Form target encoder, predictor in representation space and energy head E(intent, P), with anti-collapse measures, an embedding-space versus token-space loss ablation, and model cards with measured training energy.</li>
      <li><strong>W3. Checker-constrained decoder.</strong> Grammar-constrained candidate Forms ranked by energy and submitted to the checker, requires-change diagnostics, each naming its rule, fed back under a fixed retry budget; the checker is the sole acceptance authority with no bypass path to the engine.</li>
      <li><strong>W4. Intent-to-Form benchmark.</strong> Unit and composite tasks, the reference apps (game engine, text editor, video player, chat app, browser, terminal) and RCEdb; each task has intent, reference Form, replay traces and an equivalent source-language task for the baseline; held-out split.</li>
      <li><strong>W5. Evaluation harness with energy in joules.</strong> Both arms on identical hardware and tasks; pass@1, pass@k, ρ, C<sub>check</sub>, J<sub>acc</sub>, K<sub>acc</sub>, retries per acceptance, energy-ranking AUROC; rootless counters (<code>reported_j</code>), idle-drift Falsifier 6 gating, raw logs kept, unavailable cloud counters reported as <code>not_available</code> rather than estimated.</li>
      <li><strong>W6. Research article.</strong> This case expanded with results for H1 to H15, including negative results, figures, tables and reproducibility instructions.</li>
      <li><strong>W7. Open artifacts.</strong> Public: the Form specification, the reference checker and its emitters, benchmark tasks and traces, harness, dataset and model cards, and weights where licences allow. A number is reported only when everything needed to reproduce it is public.</li>
      <li><strong>W8. Demo.</strong> Stated intent to predicted Form to checker verdict (including a shown requires-change verdict) to replay and emitted code in two languages by the reference checker, with an on-screen joule reading.</li>
    </ul>

